						apex acute to (sub)acuminate or to obtuse, 
						base acute (to attenuate or to obtuse), 
						margin crenate-serrate, scabridulous to smooth, sparsely short-pubescent above, minutely puberulous with uncinate hairs and short-pubescent mainly on the main veins beneath; 

					secondary veins 2(-3) pairs.

Leaves opposite, those of a pair often unequal in size and shape; 
					stipules connate; 
					blade with pinnate, sub-triplinerved or single-nerved venation.

Leaves of a pair on the trailing stems (sub)equal, on the ascending stems and branches very unequal; 
